00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:31,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:32,470 --> 00:00:39,477
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:00:41,146 --> 00:00:44,899
‎2026

3
00:00:46,693 --> 00:00:47,694
‎All right.

4
00:00:47,777 --> 00:00:49,737
‎Let's raise a glass to our artist,

5
00:00:49,821 --> 00:00:52,657
‎who gave yet another
‎wonderful performance today.

6
00:00:53,825 --> 00:00:55,660
‎And congratulations to Jae-in

7
00:00:55,743 --> 00:00:58,788
‎on taking her first successful step
‎as Pi-o's new manager.

8
00:01:06,921 --> 00:01:09,132
‎I'm glad everything ended well,

9
00:01:09,674 --> 00:01:11,968
‎but do you have any idea
‎how much you scared me?

10
00:01:13,052 --> 00:01:14,929
‎You took ten years off my life.

11
00:01:15,597 --> 00:01:17,348
‎This is all thanks to Jae-in.

12
00:01:17,974 --> 00:01:18,892
‎You know,

13
00:01:18,975 --> 00:01:22,478
‎I'm much more at ease
‎knowing you're Pi-o's manager.

14
00:01:23,396 --> 00:01:25,315
‎I know how difficult it must be.

15
00:01:25,398 --> 00:01:26,816
‎I feel so bad.

16
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:28,776
‎Tell me about it, Ms. Kang.

17
00:01:29,777 --> 00:01:31,571
‎He's lucky I'm a die-hard fan.

18
00:01:32,155 --> 00:01:32,989
‎Jeez.

19
00:01:33,656 --> 00:01:37,827
‎I just remind myself how few people
‎get to turn their passion into a career.

20
00:01:38,703 --> 00:01:39,579
‎It's how I cope.

21
00:01:40,747 --> 00:01:43,708
‎But if he gives me a really hard time,

22
00:01:43,791 --> 00:01:45,376
‎you'll scold him, right?

23
00:01:45,460 --> 00:01:46,628
‎Of course.

24
00:01:47,337 --> 00:01:49,756
‎How are things looking
‎for the Esplanade concert?

25
00:01:49,839 --> 00:01:51,633
‎All seats are sold out,

26
00:01:51,716 --> 00:01:54,302
‎but there are requests
‎for additional VIP tickets,

27
00:01:54,385 --> 00:01:56,804
‎so we're coordinating
‎with the agency in Singapore.

28
00:01:57,931 --> 00:01:59,432
‎Excuse me for a moment.

29
00:01:59,515 --> 00:02:00,391
‎Sure.

30
00:02:04,354 --> 00:02:07,398
‎The schedule is tight between
‎the Vienna and Singapore concerts.

31
00:02:13,112 --> 00:02:14,113
‎Pardon me.

32
00:02:14,197 --> 00:02:15,031
‎Kang Pi-o?

33
00:02:17,575 --> 00:02:18,785
‎Hey, it really is you.

34
00:02:19,535 --> 00:02:20,495
‎It's been a while.

35
00:02:21,329 --> 00:02:23,122
‎I've seen you on the news occasionally.

36
00:02:23,665 --> 00:02:25,041
‎You know how I've been, right?

37
00:02:28,753 --> 00:02:31,297
‎By the way,
‎about that Choi Jeong-yo rumor…

38
00:02:32,590 --> 00:02:33,800
‎What's the deal with that?

39
00:02:34,801 --> 00:02:36,636
‎People say you were behind it.

40
00:02:42,058 --> 00:02:44,769
‎Your nasty personality
‎hasn't changed at all.

41
00:02:45,353 --> 00:02:46,187
‎What?

42
00:02:59,575 --> 00:03:01,494
‎What's wrong with your pinky finger?

43
00:03:03,246 --> 00:03:05,832
‎If you keep playing, you'll destroy it.

44
00:03:06,958 --> 00:03:09,210
‎Give practice a rest
‎and ‎get ‎it ‎treated ‎first.

45
00:03:15,299 --> 00:03:20,221
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

46
00:03:20,805 --> 00:03:22,598
‎EPISODE 6

47
00:04:50,978 --> 00:04:51,813
‎Hey.

48
00:04:53,481 --> 00:04:55,233
‎Guess where I am?

49
00:04:59,362 --> 00:05:00,238
‎Turn around.

50
00:05:03,825 --> 00:05:04,784
‎Ta-da.

51
00:05:08,788 --> 00:05:09,705
‎This is nice.

52
00:05:12,291 --> 00:05:16,587
‎Why do I never get bored
‎listening to you perform?

53
00:05:18,005 --> 00:05:21,592
‎Moments like this
‎make me so glad to be your manager.

54
00:05:23,845 --> 00:05:25,805
‎Can you stop saying things like that?

55
00:05:25,888 --> 00:05:26,889
‎It's not funny.

56
00:05:27,557 --> 00:05:28,891
‎What do you mean?

57
00:05:29,851 --> 00:05:33,563
‎How many people out there can watch
‎a million-dollar performance

58
00:05:33,646 --> 00:05:36,149
‎from the front row
‎without fighting for tickets?

59
00:05:40,611 --> 00:05:41,612
‎Hey.

60
00:05:42,446 --> 00:05:43,573
‎Tell me the truth.

61
00:05:44,448 --> 00:05:45,449
‎You actually love

62
00:05:46,826 --> 00:05:49,162
‎that I'm your manager, right?

63
00:05:50,705 --> 00:05:51,747
‎I do.

64
00:05:51,831 --> 00:05:53,416
‎And you like how

65
00:05:54,417 --> 00:05:56,169
‎I show up unannounced, right?

66
00:05:56,752 --> 00:05:57,712
‎I do.

67
00:05:59,547 --> 00:06:02,008
‎Then when are you going to marry me?

68
00:06:02,091 --> 00:06:02,925
‎I…

69
00:06:04,510 --> 00:06:07,138
‎Jeez, aren't you tired of this?

70
00:06:09,056 --> 00:06:09,932
‎Hey!

71
00:06:10,975 --> 00:06:13,144
‎Isn't it time you caved in?

72
00:06:14,270 --> 00:06:17,690
‎Don't tell me
‎you're married to music or something.

73
00:06:18,232 --> 00:06:19,942
‎There's your answer, so stop asking.

74
00:06:20,526 --> 00:06:22,320
‎Seriously, why do I even like him?

75
00:06:24,238 --> 00:06:25,156
‎Wait for me!

76
00:06:26,115 --> 00:06:27,033
‎Hurry up.

77
00:06:33,789 --> 00:06:37,376
‎Now, let's ask some questions
‎to the star of the competition

78
00:06:37,460 --> 00:06:39,295
‎and the most renowned pianist,

79
00:06:39,378 --> 00:06:40,588
‎Mr. Pi-o Kang!

80
00:06:45,635 --> 00:06:48,721
‎Ever since the Harmonie Competition
‎nine years ago,

81
00:06:48,804 --> 00:06:52,892
‎you've been at the forefront of bringing
‎classical music to a wider audience

82
00:06:53,434 --> 00:06:56,520
‎with both undeniable skills
‎and star quality.

83
00:06:56,604 --> 00:06:57,730
‎Back then,

84
00:06:57,813 --> 00:07:00,858
‎you shocked everyone
‎by delivering an explosive performance

85
00:07:00,942 --> 00:07:02,526
‎even after breaking a nail.

86
00:07:03,069 --> 00:07:04,445
‎How did you do it?

87
00:07:05,112 --> 00:07:09,867
‎Back then, I was so focused
‎that I didn't feel any pain at all.

88
00:07:09,951 --> 00:07:12,495
‎The Harmonie Competition was a stage

89
00:07:12,578 --> 00:07:14,789
‎I dreamed of performing on.

90
00:07:14,872 --> 00:07:16,332
‎And once I was there,

91
00:07:17,750 --> 00:07:19,502
‎pain in my finger didn't matter.

92
00:07:19,585 --> 00:07:21,629
‎Wow, what was even more astonishing

93
00:07:21,712 --> 00:07:24,507
‎was your unique interpretation
‎of the set piece.

94
00:07:24,590 --> 00:07:26,217
‎To make an interpretation like that

95
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:29,303
‎and deliver such a complete performance
‎in just a week

96
00:07:29,387 --> 00:07:30,763
‎is no small achievement.

97
00:07:31,430 --> 00:07:34,559
‎How were you able to accomplish
‎such a difficult challenge?

98
00:07:36,185 --> 00:07:38,187
‎It definitely wasn't easy.

99
00:07:38,271 --> 00:07:40,147
‎The pressure was intense.

100
00:07:40,231 --> 00:07:42,400
‎I just focused on doing my best,

101
00:07:42,483 --> 00:07:44,360
‎and it led to a good result.

102
00:07:44,443 --> 00:07:47,196
‎I don't know if I could
‎ever pull that off again.

103
00:07:47,905 --> 00:07:49,782
‎Okay, now that nine years have passed,

104
00:07:49,865 --> 00:07:52,118
‎I'd like to ask you
‎a more sensitive question.

105
00:07:52,201 --> 00:07:55,621
‎At the time, the finalists
‎must have been deeply shaken

106
00:07:55,705 --> 00:07:57,832
‎by the loss of a fellow competitor.

107
00:07:57,915 --> 00:08:01,586
‎It remains an unhealed wound
‎for us on the committee as well.

108
00:08:01,669 --> 00:08:03,087
‎How did you overcome that?

109
00:08:06,215 --> 00:08:07,466
‎It's been a very long time,

110
00:08:07,550 --> 00:08:09,343
‎but life goes on,

111
00:08:09,427 --> 00:08:11,929
‎and music heals us all, right?

112
00:08:12,430 --> 00:08:16,767
‎For me, music was my healing
‎and my salvation.

113
00:08:17,351 --> 00:08:21,063
‎Come to think of it, you went to
‎the same school as that competitor, right?

114
00:08:23,482 --> 00:08:24,317
‎Yes.

115
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:26,068
‎Were you close?

116
00:08:29,572 --> 00:08:30,615
‎No.

117
00:08:30,698 --> 00:08:32,199
‎We weren't that close.

118
00:08:45,671 --> 00:08:47,423
‎Good job, Pi-o.

119
00:08:49,425 --> 00:08:52,803
‎These are all gifts
‎from your fans in Korea.

120
00:08:53,721 --> 00:08:55,306
‎Jeez, they're dedicated.

121
00:09:01,937 --> 00:09:03,356
‎MESSAGE
‎NEW NOTIFICATION

122
00:09:03,439 --> 00:09:04,815
‎MARTIN VOGEL

123
00:09:04,899 --> 00:09:07,860
‎I found someone in Romania
‎who said they saw Mr. Choi.

124
00:09:08,944 --> 00:09:09,779
‎Jae-in.

125
00:09:11,072 --> 00:09:12,490
‎-I'll be right back.
‎-Okay.

126
00:09:21,916 --> 00:09:22,875
‎Yes, Mr. Kang?

127
00:09:24,418 --> 00:09:25,711
‎What do you mean?

128
00:09:26,462 --> 00:09:28,047
‎Who is that person?

129
00:09:28,130 --> 00:09:30,549
‎His name is Farid, and he's a refugee.

130
00:09:31,175 --> 00:09:32,802
‎When I asked for Mr. Choi's whereabouts,

131
00:09:32,885 --> 00:09:35,513
‎he demanded money
‎in exchange for the information.

132
00:09:35,596 --> 00:09:37,139
‎Should I pay him and get more out of him?

133
00:09:37,723 --> 00:09:38,641
‎No.

134
00:09:39,141 --> 00:09:41,018
‎I'd like to ask him myself.

135
00:09:47,483 --> 00:09:48,484
‎Let's go.

136
00:09:50,319 --> 00:09:51,987
‎I can't make it to the party tonight.

137
00:09:52,071 --> 00:09:53,781
‎What?

138
00:09:53,864 --> 00:09:56,909
‎You said you'd go as a favor to me.

139
00:09:57,410 --> 00:09:58,661
‎It's just…

140
00:09:59,412 --> 00:10:03,249
‎A professor I've wanted to meet
‎said they could spare time tomorrow,

141
00:10:03,332 --> 00:10:05,000
‎so I have to head to Münster.

142
00:10:06,544 --> 00:10:07,753
‎Okay then.

143
00:10:09,630 --> 00:10:11,882
‎But you'll come
‎to the promotion party, right?

144
00:10:11,966 --> 00:10:14,218
‎You really can't miss out on that.

145
00:10:15,052 --> 00:10:17,012
‎Okay. See you when I get back.

146
00:10:30,276 --> 00:10:32,027
‎Václav Havel Airport, please.

147
00:10:46,584 --> 00:10:47,418
‎Pi-o.

148
00:10:47,501 --> 00:10:49,336
‎I enjoyed watching your gala performance.

149
00:10:49,837 --> 00:10:51,505
‎You should've smiled when taking a bow.

150
00:10:51,589 --> 00:10:53,007
‎You're not sick, are you?

151
00:11:03,309 --> 00:11:05,978
‎We will now begin the appointment ceremony

152
00:11:06,061 --> 00:11:08,981
‎for new NCAPF Steering Committee members.

153
00:11:11,233 --> 00:11:13,152
‎2026 NCAPF STEERING COMMITTEE MEMBER
‎APPOINTMENT CEREMONY

154
00:11:13,235 --> 00:11:16,530
‎"You are hereby appointed
‎as a member of the Music Division

155
00:11:16,614 --> 00:11:19,241
‎of the NCAPF Steering Committee."

156
00:11:19,325 --> 00:11:22,453
‎"Presented by Kim Tae-seong,
‎Minister of Culture, Sports, and Tourism."

157
00:11:27,249 --> 00:11:28,375
‎Thank you.

158
00:11:28,876 --> 00:11:31,086
‎You're really something else.

159
00:11:31,170 --> 00:11:33,130
‎How did you manage to beat
‎all those competitors

160
00:11:33,214 --> 00:11:35,049
‎and secure a spot
‎on the committee so quickly?

161
00:11:35,132 --> 00:11:36,050
‎CERTIFICATE OF APPOINTMENT

162
00:11:36,133 --> 00:11:39,053
‎We're friends, but I seriously admire you.

163
00:11:39,136 --> 00:11:40,596
‎Oh, please.

164
00:11:40,679 --> 00:11:42,306
‎I was just next in line.

165
00:11:43,641 --> 00:11:45,935
‎So, Committee Member Kang,
‎what's first on the agenda today?

166
00:11:46,018 --> 00:11:48,395
‎Well, work starts next week.

167
00:11:48,479 --> 00:11:52,107
‎Today, I'm observing
‎the gifted school audition panel.

168
00:11:53,150 --> 00:11:53,984
‎Really?

169
00:11:54,068 --> 00:11:57,238
‎Did you notice anyone
‎worth ‎recommending ‎to ‎us?

170
00:11:57,321 --> 00:11:58,781
‎It still kills me

171
00:11:58,864 --> 00:12:01,075
‎that I lost Park Se-jin
‎to Namu Productions.

172
00:12:01,158 --> 00:12:04,161
‎I'll have to watch his audition,
‎but maybe Gam U-jin?

173
00:12:04,828 --> 00:12:06,121
‎He seems pretty good.

174
00:12:07,331 --> 00:12:08,791
‎Oh, Gam U-jin?

175
00:12:08,874 --> 00:12:11,085
‎Why? You don't like him?

176
00:12:11,168 --> 00:12:13,087
‎I know he's good,

177
00:12:13,629 --> 00:12:14,547
‎but his looks are…

178
00:12:15,839 --> 00:12:18,300
‎Hey, you need to choose
‎based on musical talent

179
00:12:18,384 --> 00:12:19,802
‎to win awards and stay around.

180
00:12:19,885 --> 00:12:21,595
‎You're not casting an actor.

181
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:24,431
‎You don't know what you're talking about.

182
00:12:24,515 --> 00:12:28,060
‎Good looks sell tickets,
‎even if your hands shake while playing.

183
00:12:28,644 --> 00:12:30,771
‎Music is 80% about looks.

184
00:12:31,355 --> 00:12:35,484
‎Okay, I'll call you later
‎if I find someone good at the audition.

185
00:12:35,568 --> 00:12:37,570
‎You're the best.

186
00:12:37,653 --> 00:12:40,239
‎What would I do without you?

187
00:12:40,322 --> 00:12:41,490
‎Save the flattery.

188
00:12:42,950 --> 00:12:44,201
‎I'll call you later then.

189
00:12:50,249 --> 00:12:51,166
‎Ms. Kim.

190
00:12:52,626 --> 00:12:54,837
‎I think the dry cleaners made a mistake.

191
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:56,380
‎These aren't mine.

192
00:12:56,463 --> 00:12:58,591
‎Gosh, these belong to Ms. Yoon…

193
00:13:01,552 --> 00:13:04,888
‎She left five years ago.
‎Why are her clothes still here?

194
00:13:04,972 --> 00:13:05,931
‎And why, of all places,

195
00:13:07,558 --> 00:13:08,684
‎did you put them in my room?

196
00:13:09,393 --> 00:13:10,644
‎The thing is,

197
00:13:10,728 --> 00:13:12,730
‎I would've removed them if I'd seen them.

198
00:13:12,813 --> 00:13:16,150
‎It seems Ms. Lee saw them
‎hanging in Mr. Kang's closet

199
00:13:16,233 --> 00:13:17,901
‎and thought they were yours.

200
00:13:20,946 --> 00:13:22,656
‎Throw them away right now.

201
00:13:52,186 --> 00:13:55,272
‎Hyeon Seon-hwa, Lee Na-rae, and Gam U-jin.

202
00:13:55,356 --> 00:13:57,107
‎I think these three

203
00:13:57,691 --> 00:13:59,902
‎are the most promising talents.

204
00:13:59,985 --> 00:14:02,071
‎Among them, I think Gam U-jin

205
00:14:02,154 --> 00:14:06,116
‎is the top candidate
‎with the kind of talent we're looking for.

206
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:07,034
‎Just a minute.

207
00:14:07,660 --> 00:14:09,870
‎Did you say Gam U-jin?

208
00:14:11,121 --> 00:14:14,333
‎I'm not sure.
‎He seems like a bit of a risk.

209
00:14:14,416 --> 00:14:16,335
‎Yes, he has flair,

210
00:14:16,418 --> 00:14:18,462
‎but he lacks the basics.

211
00:14:18,545 --> 00:14:19,380
‎I'm concerned

212
00:14:20,089 --> 00:14:22,508
‎he might get caught up in showmanship.

213
00:14:23,008 --> 00:14:27,096
‎His mistakes are inevitable
‎because he started later than the others.

214
00:14:27,179 --> 00:14:29,390
‎When it comes to identifying
‎a gifted student,

215
00:14:29,473 --> 00:14:33,519
‎we need to look beyond the surface
‎for their underlying potential.

216
00:14:34,311 --> 00:14:35,688
‎"Beyond the surface"?

217
00:14:36,855 --> 00:14:41,110
‎You know that the first couple of years
‎for young musicians are crucial.

218
00:14:41,193 --> 00:14:44,446
‎Why should we admit a student
‎whose habits are already set

219
00:14:44,530 --> 00:14:47,491
‎into a gifted school
‎funded by taxpayer money?

220
00:14:48,325 --> 00:14:49,368
‎If that's the case,

221
00:14:49,451 --> 00:14:50,828
‎instead of Gam U-jin…

222
00:14:51,787 --> 00:14:53,330
‎I'd go with Kim Hong-gyu.

223
00:14:54,665 --> 00:14:56,291
‎I'll recommend him instead.

224
00:15:07,886 --> 00:15:08,887
‎Hyun-soo!

225
00:15:14,518 --> 00:15:15,769
‎I saw your expression earlier.

226
00:15:17,563 --> 00:15:18,439
‎What is it?

227
00:15:19,064 --> 00:15:20,899
‎You don't like who I recommended?

228
00:15:21,483 --> 00:15:22,484
‎No, I don't.

229
00:15:24,403 --> 00:15:28,282
‎Do you really think it's right
‎to let spite affect a child's future?

230
00:15:28,365 --> 00:15:29,950
‎What are you talking about?

231
00:15:30,909 --> 00:15:31,785
‎Are you saying

232
00:15:32,327 --> 00:15:36,206
‎I opposed choosing Gam U-jin
‎just to pick a fight with you?

233
00:15:43,547 --> 00:15:44,423
‎You're right.

234
00:15:45,632 --> 00:15:48,135
‎I wanted to see how you'd react.

235
00:15:49,011 --> 00:15:51,472
‎At least we're finally talking again
‎after all this time.

236
00:15:52,473 --> 00:15:54,475
‎How long are you going to act like this?

237
00:15:55,100 --> 00:15:56,101
‎Don't you think

238
00:15:56,185 --> 00:16:00,022
‎it's absurd that we ended up like this
‎because of someone else?

239
00:16:00,105 --> 00:16:01,190
‎No,

240
00:16:01,273 --> 00:16:03,192
‎it's not because of someone else.

241
00:16:05,486 --> 00:16:07,029
‎It's because of you.

242
00:16:08,030 --> 00:16:09,156
‎That's enough.

243
00:16:17,623 --> 00:16:20,542
‎ROMANIA

244
00:16:29,468 --> 00:16:30,302
‎Hello.

245
00:16:30,385 --> 00:16:31,220
‎May I help you?

246
00:16:31,804 --> 00:16:32,638
‎Sorry.

247
00:16:34,348 --> 00:16:35,599
‎Can I ask you something?

248
00:16:37,309 --> 00:16:38,185
‎Let's see…

249
00:17:11,552 --> 00:17:12,553
‎Farid, right?

250
00:17:13,846 --> 00:17:17,683
‎You mentioned seeing a homeless Asian man
‎who played the piano well

251
00:17:17,766 --> 00:17:19,309
‎three years ago, right?

252
00:17:19,935 --> 00:17:20,936
‎Yes, I did.

253
00:17:21,019 --> 00:17:22,229
‎He says he saw him.

254
00:17:23,021 --> 00:17:24,189
‎Could you tell me

255
00:17:25,315 --> 00:17:26,942
‎which of these men he was?

256
00:17:36,118 --> 00:17:37,536
‎It was this man.

257
00:17:39,329 --> 00:17:41,456
‎How did you know he played the piano well?

258
00:17:41,540 --> 00:17:43,250
‎Did you see him play?

259
00:17:45,878 --> 00:17:49,590
‎He said his dream was to become a pianist.

260
00:17:49,673 --> 00:17:52,551
‎He was heartbroken
‎that he could no longer pursue it…

261
00:17:52,634 --> 00:17:54,428
‎The man's dream was to become a pianist,

262
00:17:54,511 --> 00:17:56,930
‎but he was devastated
‎that he could no longer pursue it

263
00:17:57,014 --> 00:17:58,015
‎because…

264
00:17:59,183 --> 00:18:00,809
‎he lost the use of his right hand.

265
00:18:01,685 --> 00:18:03,395
‎He lost the use of his right hand?

266
00:18:05,689 --> 00:18:07,024
‎Did he say why?

267
00:18:07,774 --> 00:18:09,526
‎Why couldn't he use his right hand?

268
00:18:10,027 --> 00:18:11,153
‎Do you know why?

269
00:18:15,866 --> 00:18:17,242
‎He only mentioned an injury,

270
00:18:17,326 --> 00:18:19,286
‎but didn't say how or why.

271
00:18:22,664 --> 00:18:24,249
‎Where did he go after that?

272
00:18:24,833 --> 00:18:26,376
‎Where did he go after that?

273
00:18:27,669 --> 00:18:28,795
‎I'm sorry.

274
00:18:28,879 --> 00:18:30,839
‎I haven't gotten my fix.

275
00:18:30,923 --> 00:18:32,007
‎If you give me some money…

276
00:18:32,966 --> 00:18:35,010
‎He's asking for money to get drugs.

277
00:18:46,146 --> 00:18:47,522
‎Give me the exact details.

278
00:18:49,066 --> 00:18:50,734
‎Where did he say he was going?

279
00:18:50,817 --> 00:18:52,319
‎Give him the exact details.

280
00:18:53,028 --> 00:18:55,447
‎Where did he say he was going?

281
00:18:55,530 --> 00:18:57,449
‎He said that

282
00:18:58,867 --> 00:19:02,996
‎he'd take a boat
‎to return to his hometown.

283
00:19:04,998 --> 00:19:06,792
‎He was going to Constanța.

284
00:19:06,875 --> 00:19:09,378
‎He was catching a boat back home

285
00:19:09,461 --> 00:19:10,963
‎and headed to Constanța.

286
00:19:11,046 --> 00:19:12,464
‎He wanted to see his mom.

287
00:19:13,090 --> 00:19:13,966
‎He said

288
00:19:14,883 --> 00:19:16,176
‎he was going to see his mom?

289
00:19:31,984 --> 00:19:33,485
‎You're looking for the pianist.

290
00:19:33,568 --> 00:19:35,821
‎He hasn't been here for two weeks.

291
00:19:35,904 --> 00:19:38,115
‎I saw him two weeks ago.
‎He was definitely here.

292
00:19:38,198 --> 00:19:40,242
‎Not this man though. No, no.

293
00:19:40,325 --> 00:19:42,369
‎But this man. He was definitely here.

294
00:19:42,452 --> 00:19:45,664
‎This one here. It was definitely this man.

295
00:19:45,747 --> 00:19:47,040
‎He was Korean,

296
00:19:47,124 --> 00:19:48,834
‎but he wasn't a pianist.

297
00:19:48,917 --> 00:19:50,335
‎What did he say?

298
00:19:50,419 --> 00:19:52,045
‎He was Korean,

299
00:19:53,255 --> 00:19:54,548
‎but not a pianist.

300
00:20:14,901 --> 00:20:17,446
‎How long are you going to
‎keep chasing false leads?

301
00:20:18,905 --> 00:20:20,449
‎It's been five whole years.

302
00:20:21,658 --> 00:20:24,453
‎Shouldn't you have found a clue by now?

303
00:20:27,497 --> 00:20:29,958
‎I'm not asking you to catch the suspects.

304
00:20:30,042 --> 00:20:31,752
‎I just want to know if he's alive.

305
00:20:33,795 --> 00:20:34,921
‎Is that so hard?

306
00:20:36,214 --> 00:20:38,258
‎Do you think it'd be easy for me
‎to find a victim

307
00:20:38,842 --> 00:20:40,510
‎that not even Interpol could find?

308
00:20:42,304 --> 00:20:45,098
‎Do you want to stop looking?

309
00:20:47,434 --> 00:20:50,020
‎I'm losing face over this too.

310
00:20:50,103 --> 00:20:53,065
‎Interpol has already concluded
‎that Mr. Choi is deceased,

311
00:20:53,148 --> 00:20:55,525
‎and we've searched every possible place.

312
00:20:56,234 --> 00:20:58,070
‎Honestly, all that's missing is the body.

313
00:20:58,153 --> 00:21:00,697
‎The odds of Mr. Choi being alive
‎are close to zero.

314
00:21:04,826 --> 00:21:06,703
‎What exactly are you trying to confirm?

315
00:21:08,413 --> 00:21:10,207
‎Proof that Mr. Choi is alive?

316
00:21:11,166 --> 00:21:12,376
‎Or proof of his death?

317
00:21:24,513 --> 00:21:25,597
‎Cheers.

318
00:22:15,605 --> 00:22:17,524
‎What exactly are you trying to confirm?

319
00:22:18,775 --> 00:22:20,360
‎Proof that Mr. Choi is alive?

320
00:22:21,027 --> 00:22:22,404
‎Or proof of his death?

321
00:22:42,716 --> 00:22:43,550
‎Hey.

322
00:22:43,633 --> 00:22:46,219
‎Hey, where are you?

323
00:22:46,303 --> 00:22:49,389
‎I told you to come to the party,
‎but you're not here.

324
00:22:49,973 --> 00:22:51,558
‎Oh, sorry.

325
00:22:53,059 --> 00:22:54,269
‎It slipped my mind.

326
00:22:54,352 --> 00:22:56,021
‎Have you been drinking?

327
00:23:01,526 --> 00:23:02,527
‎A little.

328
00:23:02,611 --> 00:23:04,321
‎Where are you?

329
00:23:21,504 --> 00:23:22,547
‎Pi-o!

330
00:23:23,757 --> 00:23:25,175
‎What's going on?

331
00:23:25,258 --> 00:23:26,134
‎What happened?

332
00:23:30,222 --> 00:23:31,097
‎You're here.

333
00:23:31,181 --> 00:23:32,807
‎Did something happen?

334
00:23:34,434 --> 00:23:36,937
‎Why did you drink so much?

335
00:23:38,521 --> 00:23:39,439
‎Nothing happened.

336
00:23:41,316 --> 00:23:42,192
‎Hey.

337
00:23:42,859 --> 00:23:44,611
‎Hey, Pi-o!

338
00:23:46,154 --> 00:23:48,740
‎This isn't like you at all.

339
00:23:50,659 --> 00:23:52,494
‎Pull yourself together, will you?

340
00:23:53,703 --> 00:23:54,579
‎We're almost there.

341
00:23:56,998 --> 00:23:57,916
‎No.

342
00:23:58,500 --> 00:23:59,751
‎I'm fine.

343
00:23:59,834 --> 00:24:00,919
‎You can go now.

344
00:24:01,002 --> 00:24:02,629
‎I can walk on my own.

345
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:05,131
‎You'll hurt yourself.

346
00:24:08,093 --> 00:24:09,052
‎Where's your room key?

347
00:24:25,235 --> 00:24:26,319
‎Jae-in.

348
00:24:27,862 --> 00:24:28,905
‎I'm sorry,

349
00:24:30,532 --> 00:24:33,326
‎but can you stay with me
‎until I fall asleep?

350
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:35,996
‎What?

351
00:24:38,498 --> 00:24:41,835
‎You won't accept my feelings for you,
‎but you'll ask me to do that?

352
00:24:43,461 --> 00:24:44,796
‎You're so selfish.

353
00:24:47,632 --> 00:24:49,009
‎You're the only person…

354
00:24:52,304 --> 00:24:53,638
‎I can trust in the world.

355
00:24:58,852 --> 00:25:00,103
‎Do you still…

356
00:25:01,271 --> 00:25:03,356
‎have trouble sleeping?

357
00:25:04,941 --> 00:25:05,817
‎Yeah.

358
00:25:07,027 --> 00:25:08,528
‎I wish I could stop thinking…

359
00:25:11,906 --> 00:25:13,116
‎and sleep soundly.

360
00:25:15,160 --> 00:25:16,786
‎I told you not to push yourself

361
00:25:18,163 --> 00:25:19,456
‎and to get some rest.

362
00:25:20,874 --> 00:25:22,667
‎How about scaling back performances

363
00:25:23,293 --> 00:25:25,879
‎and taking a year off?

364
00:25:30,008 --> 00:25:31,009
‎We'll see.

365
00:25:32,177 --> 00:25:33,595
‎Don't try so hard.

366
00:25:34,220 --> 00:25:37,265
‎You're doing really well as it is.

367
00:25:39,392 --> 00:25:40,643
‎Pi-o.

368
00:25:41,978 --> 00:25:44,981
‎There's something I want to tell you.

369
00:25:46,066 --> 00:25:46,983
‎Go ahead.

370
00:25:49,569 --> 00:25:50,862
‎It's just that…

371
00:25:53,031 --> 00:25:55,325
‎You know that I really like you…

372
00:25:57,535 --> 00:25:58,620
‎don't you?

373
00:25:59,621 --> 00:26:00,955
‎I do.

374
00:26:01,748 --> 00:26:02,957
‎No.

375
00:26:03,541 --> 00:26:04,626
‎You have no idea.

376
00:26:09,881 --> 00:26:10,799
‎To be honest…

377
00:26:14,052 --> 00:26:18,890
‎I've been playing it off like a joke
‎every time I confessed my feelings to you,

378
00:26:20,934 --> 00:26:23,269
‎but I meant it every time.

379
00:26:42,997 --> 00:26:45,208
‎Just take care of your health, Pi-o.

380
00:27:14,237 --> 00:27:16,156
‎I received word that the suspect

381
00:27:16,239 --> 00:27:18,825
‎who abducted Mr. Choi
‎was released from Rezina Penitentiary.

382
00:27:23,997 --> 00:27:25,415
‎What do you mean?

383
00:27:26,082 --> 00:27:27,375
‎You found the suspect?

384
00:27:27,876 --> 00:27:31,713
‎MOLDOVA

385
00:27:38,803 --> 00:27:40,305
‎His name is Andrei Ceban.

386
00:27:41,389 --> 00:27:44,434
‎He's 48 years old and from Transnistria.

387
00:27:45,018 --> 00:27:46,227
‎He's a former mercenary

388
00:27:46,853 --> 00:27:50,732
‎who just got released from prison
‎after serving time for assault.

389
00:27:51,691 --> 00:27:53,985
‎No wonder I couldn't find him anywhere.

390
00:27:54,068 --> 00:27:55,487
‎He was locked up.

391
00:27:57,864 --> 00:27:59,324
‎Can I ask you something?

392
00:27:59,908 --> 00:28:02,535
‎You said no questions,
‎so I've been holding back.

393
00:28:03,203 --> 00:28:06,748
‎Why are you so determined
‎to find Mr. Choi?

394
00:28:07,582 --> 00:28:09,209
‎At this point, even family gives up.

395
00:28:12,504 --> 00:28:16,132
‎Is Mr. Choi really that important to you?

396
00:28:42,116 --> 00:28:43,576
‎Hey, hey. Where are you going?

397
00:28:43,660 --> 00:28:45,119
‎Is Andrei Ceban here?

398
00:28:45,870 --> 00:28:47,455
‎-Your name?
‎-Oh, it's Vogel.

399
00:28:47,539 --> 00:28:49,666
‎-That guy. He's coming in too.
‎-Wait a moment.

400
00:28:54,712 --> 00:28:55,547
‎Okay?

401
00:28:57,090 --> 00:28:57,924
‎Hey.

402
00:29:16,025 --> 00:29:17,819
‎Hello.

403
00:29:18,444 --> 00:29:19,320
‎Andrei.

404
00:29:19,821 --> 00:29:22,740
‎We came to ask a few questions.

405
00:29:54,731 --> 00:29:56,024
‎Nine years ago

406
00:29:56,649 --> 00:29:58,318
‎at the Harmonie Competition,

407
00:29:59,110 --> 00:30:01,738
‎are you the one who abducted this man?

408
00:30:08,411 --> 00:30:10,079
‎Who the hell is asking?

409
00:30:17,921 --> 00:30:19,505
‎I remember you.

410
00:30:20,798 --> 00:30:23,927
‎You're the guy
‎who won that competition, right?

411
00:30:24,594 --> 00:30:28,640
‎The one who benefited the most
‎from that… mess.

412
00:30:31,225 --> 00:30:32,185
‎Let me ask you again.

413
00:30:33,895 --> 00:30:37,148
‎You abducted Jeong-yo Choi, right?

414
00:30:37,231 --> 00:30:38,900
‎What's in it for me?

415
00:30:44,614 --> 00:30:47,450
‎What did you do to Jeong-yo?

416
00:30:49,994 --> 00:30:51,120
‎He's dead.

417
00:30:53,498 --> 00:30:54,374
‎Dead?

418
00:30:54,457 --> 00:30:56,125
‎Yes, dead.

419
00:30:58,378 --> 00:30:59,504
‎By whom?

420
00:30:59,587 --> 00:31:00,588
‎Me.

421
00:31:05,593 --> 00:31:06,678
‎Why did you kill him?

422
00:31:09,764 --> 00:31:12,934
‎Why did you kill him?

423
00:31:14,143 --> 00:31:15,687
‎It was not the plan.

424
00:31:15,770 --> 00:31:20,191
‎The plan was to let him go
‎after we got the money.

425
00:31:20,274 --> 00:31:21,109
‎But…

426
00:31:21,985 --> 00:31:24,320
‎he put up a bit too much of a fight.

427
00:31:24,404 --> 00:31:25,446
‎Was it for money?

428
00:31:25,530 --> 00:31:27,699
‎Did you abduct him for that reason
‎or did someone--

429
00:31:27,782 --> 00:31:28,783
‎Enough.

430
00:31:29,701 --> 00:31:30,743
‎You want to know?

431
00:31:32,954 --> 00:31:34,455
‎Three million lei.

432
00:31:35,498 --> 00:31:36,541
‎Then I'll tell you.

433
00:31:46,968 --> 00:31:48,386
‎Tell me now!

434
00:31:48,469 --> 00:31:49,429
‎Mr. Kang, no!

435
00:31:49,512 --> 00:31:51,014
‎You killed someone over money?

436
00:31:51,097 --> 00:31:52,473
‎Do you even know how special he was?

437
00:31:52,557 --> 00:31:53,975
‎Do you have any idea?

438
00:31:54,058 --> 00:31:55,059
‎Stop!

439
00:32:12,869 --> 00:32:14,787
‎Do you know who we are?

440
00:32:15,496 --> 00:32:16,372
‎You little…

441
00:32:18,041 --> 00:32:18,875
‎Huh?

442
00:32:19,375 --> 00:32:20,626
‎You know what?

443
00:32:21,419 --> 00:32:24,213
‎Now, six million.

444
00:32:25,048 --> 00:32:26,049
‎Then I'll tell you.

445
00:32:53,868 --> 00:32:55,995
‎Where's the nearest international bank?

446
00:32:56,579 --> 00:32:57,413
‎What?

447
00:32:57,997 --> 00:32:59,082
‎You want to come back here?

448
00:33:22,105 --> 00:33:23,147
‎What is that?

449
00:33:23,231 --> 00:33:24,232
‎What's going on?

450
00:33:33,574 --> 00:33:37,036
‎POLICE

451
00:33:46,838 --> 00:33:47,922
‎What happened?

452
00:33:50,341 --> 00:33:51,259
‎They say

453
00:33:52,260 --> 00:33:53,136
‎Andrei is dead.

454
00:33:54,095 --> 00:33:55,304
‎He's dead?

455
00:33:55,388 --> 00:33:58,307
‎He got into a fight with someone
‎and was killed.

456
00:34:00,226 --> 00:34:01,227
‎No.

457
00:34:01,310 --> 00:34:03,229
‎Mr. Kang. Wait!

458
00:34:04,438 --> 00:34:06,315
‎Look, Mr. Kang. Hey!

459
00:34:07,525 --> 00:34:08,609
‎Wait a minute!

460
00:34:40,725 --> 00:34:41,642
‎Are you okay?

461
00:34:44,896 --> 00:34:46,564
‎Well, I guess this is it for me.

462
00:34:47,648 --> 00:34:48,983
‎But I'm sure Mr. Choi

463
00:34:50,193 --> 00:34:51,777
‎is smiling down from up above,

464
00:34:52,653 --> 00:34:56,032
‎knowing he has a friend
‎who searched for him for so long.

465
00:34:56,741 --> 00:34:58,117
‎So I hope

466
00:34:59,744 --> 00:35:01,162
‎you'll move on from the one you lost…

467
00:35:04,957 --> 00:35:06,459
‎and find happiness.

468
00:35:13,007 --> 00:35:14,258
‎Thank you for everything.

469
00:35:46,832 --> 00:35:48,542
‎Hey, Kang Pi-o.

470
00:35:49,126 --> 00:35:51,587
‎Where are you? Why aren't you back yet?

471
00:35:52,505 --> 00:35:54,715
‎You said you'd watch U-hyeok play.

472
00:35:56,050 --> 00:35:59,178
‎The little punk made it to the semifinals.

473
00:36:00,554 --> 00:36:01,681
‎Where are you?

474
00:36:01,764 --> 00:36:02,932
‎Your place in Berlin?

475
00:36:03,474 --> 00:36:04,642
‎No.

476
00:36:05,434 --> 00:36:06,936
‎I'm in Moldova.

477
00:36:07,436 --> 00:36:08,938
‎What? Moldova?

478
00:36:10,022 --> 00:36:11,023
‎Hey.

479
00:36:12,108 --> 00:36:13,943
‎What's wrong with your voice?

480
00:36:15,569 --> 00:36:16,821
‎Are you sick?

481
00:36:20,908 --> 00:36:21,826
‎Pi-o.

482
00:36:23,536 --> 00:36:24,537
‎Hey.

483
00:36:25,037 --> 00:36:26,998
‎What are you doing here like this?

484
00:36:27,957 --> 00:36:29,083
‎You should've gone to a doctor.

485
00:36:30,835 --> 00:36:31,752
‎Fever medicine.

486
00:36:32,545 --> 00:36:34,380
‎-What?
‎-Get me some fever medicine.

487
00:36:34,463 --> 00:36:35,381
‎Fever medicine?

488
00:36:48,686 --> 00:36:50,229
‎Are you feeling better?

489
00:36:58,946 --> 00:37:01,449
‎I picked up some food for you.

490
00:37:01,532 --> 00:37:03,617
‎It doesn't look appetizing,

491
00:37:03,701 --> 00:37:05,911
‎but you need to eat something

492
00:37:06,787 --> 00:37:08,205
‎and get your strength back.

493
00:37:10,166 --> 00:37:11,000
‎Thanks.

494
00:37:26,182 --> 00:37:28,476
‎Sorry I keep troubling you.

495
00:37:30,061 --> 00:37:30,895
‎So…

496
00:37:32,021 --> 00:37:34,857
‎Why did you come all the way here?

497
00:37:36,650 --> 00:37:37,735
‎Hey.

498
00:37:37,818 --> 00:37:39,862
‎Are you hiding something from me?

499
00:37:41,947 --> 00:37:43,949
‎I came to find Jeong-yo.

500
00:37:44,533 --> 00:37:45,368
‎What?

501
00:37:46,243 --> 00:37:48,245
‎Someone told me the suspect

502
00:37:48,829 --> 00:37:50,748
‎who abducted Jeong-yo was here.

503
00:37:56,087 --> 00:37:56,962
‎And?

504
00:37:57,797 --> 00:37:58,798
‎He's dead.

505
00:38:01,300 --> 00:38:02,134
‎What?

506
00:38:02,218 --> 00:38:03,803
‎He had already died…

507
00:38:06,180 --> 00:38:07,264
‎nine years ago.

508
00:38:10,893 --> 00:38:13,062
‎I hoped he was still alive.

509
00:38:14,271 --> 00:38:15,189
‎I prayed…

510
00:38:18,275 --> 00:38:20,403
‎he wasn't dead.

511
00:38:22,196 --> 00:38:24,240
‎I can't ask for his forgiveness now.

512
00:38:27,910 --> 00:38:29,370
‎There's no way to set things right.

513
00:38:30,621 --> 00:38:32,498
‎It's time to move on.

514
00:38:33,207 --> 00:38:35,000
‎It happened so long ago, so why--

515
00:38:35,084 --> 00:38:37,336
‎Because I stole Jeong-yo's place.

516
00:38:38,212 --> 00:38:40,464
‎What kind of nonsense is that?

517
00:38:42,091 --> 00:38:43,926
‎You performed really well back then,

518
00:38:44,635 --> 00:38:47,221
‎which is why no one
‎could argue with the results.

519
00:38:48,597 --> 00:38:50,307
‎Even if Jeong-yo had been there,

520
00:38:51,267 --> 00:38:52,726
‎you would've won first place.

521
00:38:53,310 --> 00:38:54,228
‎No.

522
00:38:57,440 --> 00:38:58,649
‎This place was never mine.

523
00:39:00,526 --> 00:39:01,610
‎But now,

524
00:39:02,570 --> 00:39:04,530
‎it's too late to set things right.

525
00:39:24,133 --> 00:39:25,384
‎You should've told me.

526
00:39:27,636 --> 00:39:28,762
‎If you were struggling…

527
00:39:30,973 --> 00:39:32,808
‎you should've told me.

528
00:39:43,360 --> 00:39:45,404
‎Let's move on, Pi-o.

529
00:39:46,697 --> 00:39:47,656
‎It's time…

530
00:39:49,366 --> 00:39:50,659
‎to say goodbye to Jeong-yo.

531
00:39:52,411 --> 00:39:53,621
‎That's what Jeong-yo

532
00:39:54,747 --> 00:39:56,332
‎would want you to do.

533
00:40:00,252 --> 00:40:01,504
‎He'd want you to become

534
00:40:03,255 --> 00:40:05,674
‎an amazing pianist in his place.

535
00:40:31,408 --> 00:40:33,452
‎I'll never leave you.

536
00:40:59,353 --> 00:41:00,437
‎I'll see you there.

537
00:41:02,189 --> 00:41:03,774
‎Try not to cry when you miss me.

538
00:41:06,443 --> 00:41:07,319
‎Hey.

539
00:41:08,320 --> 00:41:11,073
‎Are you still going to
‎make this feel like a one-sided crush?

540
00:41:14,743 --> 00:41:15,703
‎I'll be going.

541
00:41:16,620 --> 00:41:17,454
‎Okay.

542
00:41:22,084 --> 00:41:23,002
‎Bye.

543
00:41:57,703 --> 00:41:58,537
‎Pi-o!

544
00:41:59,913 --> 00:42:01,206
‎I'll take that.

545
00:42:02,666 --> 00:42:05,127
‎I told you not to come get me.

546
00:42:05,210 --> 00:42:08,380
‎How could I not?
‎I haven't seen you in six months.

547
00:42:08,464 --> 00:42:10,174
‎I missed you so much that I almost cried.

548
00:42:10,758 --> 00:42:13,427
‎I watched the Prague gala performance.
‎You were amazing.

549
00:42:13,510 --> 00:42:15,220
‎Did you do well at the Berlin concert too?

550
00:42:16,680 --> 00:42:17,514
‎Yes.

551
00:42:36,450 --> 00:42:37,743
‎Welcome back, Pi-o.

552
00:42:38,327 --> 00:42:39,411
‎How have you been?

553
00:42:40,079 --> 00:42:42,414
‎Can you get Pi-o's luggage from the trunk?

554
00:42:42,498 --> 00:42:43,332
‎Where's Father?

555
00:42:54,176 --> 00:42:55,010
‎Father.

556
00:42:55,511 --> 00:42:56,845
‎Pi-o's back.

557
00:43:04,353 --> 00:43:06,313
‎How have you been, Grandfather?

558
00:43:13,987 --> 00:43:16,448
‎Your only grandson is back
‎after six months.

559
00:43:16,532 --> 00:43:18,325
‎Will you at least answer him?

560
00:43:18,409 --> 00:43:19,368
‎Move.

561
00:43:22,746 --> 00:43:25,124
‎You're blocking the wind. Move.

562
00:43:34,758 --> 00:43:35,592
‎Let's go.

563
00:43:43,684 --> 00:43:45,477
‎That stubborn old man.

564
00:43:45,561 --> 00:43:47,896
‎I thought he'd mellow out as he got older,

565
00:43:47,980 --> 00:43:49,606
‎but he hasn't changed a bit.

566
00:43:50,482 --> 00:43:51,650
‎Don't worry about it.

567
00:43:52,151 --> 00:43:53,318
‎I'm fine.

568
00:44:56,256 --> 00:44:58,467
‎I'VE MEMORIZED EVERYTHING.
‎TAKE IT IF YOU NEED IT!

569
00:45:23,825 --> 00:45:25,369
‎There you are, Pi-o!

570
00:45:25,452 --> 00:45:26,995
‎How have you been, Ms. Han?

571
00:45:27,704 --> 00:45:30,165
‎Not very well because I missed you.

572
00:45:30,666 --> 00:45:33,335
‎Going to your performances
‎was my favorite thing,

573
00:45:33,418 --> 00:45:35,003
‎but I've been too busy to go.

574
00:45:36,922 --> 00:45:39,716
‎By the way, why do you look so worn out?

575
00:45:39,800 --> 00:45:41,009
‎Did something happen?

576
00:45:42,135 --> 00:45:43,136
‎No.

577
00:45:44,596 --> 00:45:46,557
‎Well, your album is out now.

578
00:45:50,310 --> 00:45:52,229
‎What do you think? It's nice, right?

579
00:45:54,648 --> 00:45:58,360
‎We should probably plan a recital tour
‎around the release.

580
00:45:58,902 --> 00:46:00,696
‎Which cities do you want to perform in?

581
00:46:01,613 --> 00:46:03,865
‎The usual ones, I guess.

582
00:46:05,534 --> 00:46:09,121
‎I'm thinking Seoul, Incheon,
‎Daejeon, Daegu, Busan,

583
00:46:09,204 --> 00:46:12,124
‎and Tongyeong to start with.

584
00:46:12,708 --> 00:46:14,501
‎What do you think? Is that too many?

585
00:46:14,585 --> 00:46:16,086
‎Should we just choose four?

586
00:46:19,089 --> 00:46:21,174
‎No, it's fine.

587
00:47:31,453 --> 00:47:33,580
‎REDANOL

588
00:48:46,695 --> 00:48:47,904
‎Pi-o?

589
00:48:47,988 --> 00:48:49,072
‎KANG PI-O RECITALS

590
00:48:49,156 --> 00:48:50,198
‎Kang Pi-o!

591
00:48:50,282 --> 00:48:52,242
‎KANG'S "GASPARD DE LA NUIT" LAPSE
‎RAISES HEALTH CONCERNS

592
00:48:52,325 --> 00:48:53,660
‎Open the door.

593
00:48:53,744 --> 00:48:55,829
‎It's been days now, and you haven't eaten!

594
00:48:58,331 --> 00:49:01,001
‎You've been so busy
‎that you haven't had time to practice.

595
00:49:01,084 --> 00:49:02,878
‎You just feel a little worn out,
‎that's all.

596
00:49:03,587 --> 00:49:04,671
‎Once you rest up

597
00:49:04,755 --> 00:49:06,381
‎and get back into a routine…

598
00:49:11,553 --> 00:49:12,387
‎Pi…

599
00:49:46,004 --> 00:49:46,838
‎Pi-o.

600
00:49:48,715 --> 00:49:49,591
‎Mr. Do.

601
00:49:52,677 --> 00:49:53,762
‎Even in this state…

602
00:49:55,806 --> 00:49:56,807
‎you still can't…

603
00:49:58,350 --> 00:49:59,935
‎bear to look at me?

604
00:50:03,688 --> 00:50:05,732
‎I waited for so long…

605
00:50:08,151 --> 00:50:09,361
‎but you still can't?

606
00:50:13,323 --> 00:50:14,241
‎Why?

607
00:50:16,576 --> 00:50:19,412
‎Are you uncomfortable around me
‎because of my mom?

608
00:50:21,081 --> 00:50:23,458
‎Or is it because
‎I didn't measure up as a student?

609
00:50:23,542 --> 00:50:25,544
‎What do you mean? That's not it at all.

610
00:50:25,627 --> 00:50:26,503
‎No.

611
00:50:28,004 --> 00:50:30,423
‎Just tell me the truth.

612
00:50:31,341 --> 00:50:33,635
‎Did you ever think of me as your student?

613
00:50:33,718 --> 00:50:35,512
‎Pi-o, what are you talking about?

614
00:50:35,595 --> 00:50:36,847
‎I've really been meaning…

615
00:50:38,849 --> 00:50:40,600
‎to ask you this.

616
00:50:41,601 --> 00:50:44,437
‎Why did you have Jeong-yo and me
‎play the same piece?

617
00:50:45,397 --> 00:50:46,273
‎What?

618
00:50:46,356 --> 00:50:48,400
‎I told you I wanted to play
‎the third concerto,

619
00:50:48,483 --> 00:50:50,277
‎so why did you make me play
‎the second one?

620
00:50:50,360 --> 00:50:52,487
‎Did you do that on purpose

621
00:50:52,571 --> 00:50:54,281
‎to put our differences on display?

622
00:50:54,364 --> 00:50:57,033
‎Pi-o, you've got it all wrong.

623
00:50:58,201 --> 00:51:00,704
‎I cared for you and Jeong-yo

624
00:51:01,997 --> 00:51:03,790
‎equally as my students.

625
00:51:03,874 --> 00:51:06,835
‎Then why are you being so harsh to me?

626
00:51:07,419 --> 00:51:10,714
‎You knew how much I needed your help,

627
00:51:10,797 --> 00:51:11,756
‎so why…

628
00:51:12,966 --> 00:51:15,302
‎Why do you only feel
‎for your dead student?

629
00:51:15,385 --> 00:51:16,636
‎That's not true.

630
00:51:19,431 --> 00:51:21,308
‎I feel for you too.

631
00:51:21,391 --> 00:51:22,934
‎You weigh on my mind just as much.

632
00:51:24,936 --> 00:51:27,939
‎But I have nothing left to teach you…

633
00:51:29,816 --> 00:51:33,028
‎because you've grown into a pianist
‎with a distinct identity.

634
00:51:33,862 --> 00:51:35,864
‎I thought the best thing to do

635
00:51:37,115 --> 00:51:39,075
‎was to stand back and quietly support you.

636
00:51:39,159 --> 00:51:40,660
‎That's not true!

637
00:51:41,536 --> 00:51:43,413
‎You never liked me!

638
00:51:44,748 --> 00:51:47,626
‎Just say you didn't want
‎anything to do with a student like me.

639
00:51:48,126 --> 00:51:50,879
‎Say that my skills were pathetic
‎and I was all show!

640
00:51:51,504 --> 00:51:54,299
‎Just say you didn't want a lousy student

641
00:51:54,382 --> 00:51:56,635
‎who had no soul in his playing!

642
00:52:23,119 --> 00:52:25,288
‎THE BREAKDOWN DID NOT START ON STAGE

643
00:52:25,372 --> 00:52:27,707
‎PIANIST KANG PI-O'S DOWNFALL
‎WAS INEVITABLE

644
00:52:37,092 --> 00:52:37,926
‎Pi-o.

645
00:52:38,009 --> 00:52:39,386
‎Get up.

646
00:52:39,469 --> 00:52:41,304
‎Jae-in is here, so get up.

647
00:52:42,931 --> 00:52:44,349
‎You have a guest and you still…

648
00:52:58,947 --> 00:52:59,864
‎Pi-o.

649
00:53:01,282 --> 00:53:02,617
‎Get up and sit next to me.

650
00:53:12,544 --> 00:53:16,423
‎How long are you going to keep this up?

651
00:53:17,007 --> 00:53:19,134
‎Your life doesn't end
‎over one bad performance.

652
00:53:20,176 --> 00:53:24,055
‎If you're in a slump,
‎you need to find a way out of it.

653
00:53:24,639 --> 00:53:25,640
‎I'm sorry,

654
00:53:27,142 --> 00:53:28,268
‎but just leave me alone.

655
00:53:29,686 --> 00:53:31,771
‎I'll take care of my own business.

656
00:53:31,855 --> 00:53:35,942
‎Why don't you go on a trip
‎instead of staying in Korea?

657
00:53:36,860 --> 00:53:39,195
‎You're struggling
‎because of all the rumors

658
00:53:39,279 --> 00:53:41,072
‎and people judging you.

659
00:53:41,990 --> 00:53:44,743
‎If you go on that trip to Europe
‎you've been talking about

660
00:53:44,826 --> 00:53:46,327
‎and get some rest…

661
00:53:48,413 --> 00:53:49,998
‎Where can I hide?

662
00:53:51,541 --> 00:53:53,960
‎It won't change the fact
‎that I can't play the piano,

663
00:53:54,544 --> 00:53:56,254
‎so where am I supposed to hide?

664
00:54:03,887 --> 00:54:05,305
‎LEE BO-HUN

665
00:54:08,183 --> 00:54:10,226
‎I've been hallucinating

666
00:54:11,603 --> 00:54:12,520
‎my missing friend.

667
00:54:14,064 --> 00:54:16,024
‎I thought if I laid him to rest somehow,

668
00:54:17,484 --> 00:54:18,777
‎things would get better.

669
00:54:19,652 --> 00:54:21,112
‎But it feels like

670
00:54:22,572 --> 00:54:23,948
‎I'm completely consumed…

671
00:54:26,034 --> 00:54:27,160
‎by my dead friend.

672
00:54:28,036 --> 00:54:29,162
‎It's possible

673
00:54:29,746 --> 00:54:33,500
‎that you feel this way
‎because you haven't properly grieved.

674
00:54:33,583 --> 00:54:34,918
‎Why don't you instead

675
00:54:35,418 --> 00:54:38,421
‎take some time and face your grief?

676
00:54:39,172 --> 00:54:40,507
‎Accepting it

677
00:54:40,590 --> 00:54:43,134
‎and letting it go is the best thing to do.

678
00:58:26,524 --> 00:58:29,402
‎SPECIAL THANKS TO KO CHANG-SEOK
‎FOR HIS GUEST APPEARANCE

679
00:58:49,797 --> 00:58:51,966
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

680
00:58:52,050 --> 00:58:55,053
‎Today's winner, Luca Domenico.

681
00:58:55,136 --> 00:58:56,596
‎Choi Jeong-yo has returned.

682
00:58:56,679 --> 00:58:58,181
‎I do not wish for my music

683
00:58:58,264 --> 00:59:00,433
‎to be overshadowed by my past.

684
00:59:01,309 --> 00:59:02,810
‎I'd recognize you anywhere.

685
00:59:04,062 --> 00:59:05,188
‎It's definitely Jeong-yo.

686
00:59:06,105 --> 00:59:06,939
‎Choi Jeong-yo!

687
00:59:07,023 --> 00:59:08,358
‎Please, let me see him.

688
00:59:08,441 --> 00:59:10,443
‎Mr. Domenico says he doesn't know you.

689
00:59:10,943 --> 00:59:12,403
‎I have another request for you.

690
00:59:14,072 --> 00:59:17,241
‎Look into this quietly
‎and make sure nothing leaks.

691
00:59:20,453 --> 00:59:25,458
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim

